course: dictionary
lesson: 409
title: Who is the applicant?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An applicant is a person who asks for something, usually in writing or on a form. The thing they ask for might be a job, a place at a school, a passport or a loan. Look for the clue: is someone asking for something?
explain: «The court orders that the child shall reside with the applicant.» Reside means live. The court and the child are the clues. The applicant is the person who asked the court for this, so try it: put "the person who asked" in place of applicant, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Job adverts often use the word too: «Applicants must be over 18.» That means every person who asks for the job must be over 18. A successful applicant is the person who gets the job or the place. When the context is not enough, look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Applicant» means a person who asks for something, in writing or on a form.
fact: «Successful applicant» means the person who gets the job or place.
fact: In maths, you can count applicants: «There were 40 applicants for 5 places» means 40 people asked for a place.
fact: Common phrases: «job applicant», «successful applicant», «applicants must …».
exercise: «The court orders that the child shall reside with the applicant.» Who is the applicant? | A judge who sits in the court | *A person who asked the court for something | A house where the child lives | A bird that flies over the court
exercise: «There were 40 applicants for 5 places at the school.» How many people asked for a place? | *40 | 35 | 5 | 45
exercise: «Applicants must be over 18.» What does applicants mean here? | Shops that sell shoes | Bosses who give out jobs | *People who ask for the job | People who are older than 18
test: «She was the successful applicant, and she started work on Monday.» What does successful applicant mean? | A person who sent in a letter but was not chosen | A person who did not ask for anything | *A person who asked for the job and got it | A person who ran away from the job
test: Which word means a person who fills in a form to ask for a passport? | Judge | Tourist | Teacher | *Applicant
exam: Lexi reads «Each applicant must send a form by Friday.» What is an applicant? | *A person who asks for something on a form | A form that is sent by post | A day of the week | A teacher who marks forms
